  "body": {
    "id": "thm:face-recovery",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every \\(P\\in\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{face}}\\) satisfying \\(\\texttt{ass:no-date-one-absorption}\\), the conclusions of \\(\\texttt{thm:active-frontier-recovery}\\) upgrade throughout \\(\\mathcal F(p)\\) to\n\\[\n \\pi_j^d=\\alpha_j^d>0,\\qquad \\tau_j=\\eta_j=\\nu_j/\\pi_j^1.\n\\]\nThus the same formulas recover the full type masses, the complete component law of \\((Z,X_0,X_1,X_2,X_3)\\) in every cohort, every full conditional type effect, and the aggregate \\(\\tau\\), in the common descending signature order. The result requires neither time homogeneity nor a date-\\(4\\) common untreated kernel and permits the rank-deficient common absorbing row.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P",
      "\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{face}}",
      "p",
      "\\mathcal F(p)",
      "J",
      "j",
      "d",
      "\\pi_j^d",
      "\\alpha_j^d",
      "\\tau_j",
      "\\eta_j",
      "\\nu_j",
      "\\tau",
      "\\theta_J"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:active-frontier-recovery",
      "def:compatible-fiber",
      "ass:no-date-one-absorption",
      "ass:cohort-overlap",
      "ass:two-types",
      "ass:absorbing-exit"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(P\\) as in the statement and \\(\\widetilde P\\in\\mathcal F(p)\\). Cohort overlap and equality of every observed cell probability imply\n\\[\n \\widetilde P(X_1=e\\mid D=d)=P(X_1=e\\mid D=d)=0.          \\tag{1}\n\\]\nSince \\(Z\\) has the finite support \\(\\{1,\\ldots,J\\}\\), nonnegativity and (1) give \\(\\widetilde P(Z=j,X_1=e\\mid D=d)=0\\) for every \\(j,d\\). Therefore\n\\[\n \\widetilde\\pi_j^d=\\widetilde P(Z=j,X_1\\in\\mathcal A\\mid D=d)\n =\\widetilde\\alpha_j^d.                                  \\tag{2}\n\\]\nThe active-frontier theorem identifies the right side throughout the fiber and derives its strict positivity from anchor-star nonsingularity. Hence\n\\[\n \\widetilde\\pi_j^d=\\widetilde\\alpha_j^d=\\alpha_j^d=\\pi_j^d>0. \\tag{3}\n\\]\nThe active theorem recovers the complete unnormalized component law on \\(\\{X_1\\in\\mathcal A\\}\\). Equation (1) says this event has full probability within every positive type-cohort cell in (3), so that unnormalized law is the full component law. Dividing by the identified mass in (3) recovers its conditional version.\n\nLet \\(\\Delta=\\operatorname{onehot}(X_3(1))-\\operatorname{onehot}(X_3(0))\\). Since conditioning on \\(X_1\\in\\mathcal A\\) removes a null event within \\((D=1,Z=j)\\),\n\\[\n \\tau_j=E(\\Delta\\mid D=1,Z=j)\n =E(\\Delta\\mid D=1,Z=j,X_1\\in\\mathcal A)\n =\\eta_j=\\frac{\\nu_j}{\\alpha_j^1}=\\frac{\\nu_j}{\\pi_j^1}. \\tag{4}\n\\]\nThe aggregate equality \\(\\tau=\\sum_j\\nu_j\\) and \\(\\Phi(p)=\\theta_J\\) are already proved by the active theorem. Since the proof there uses only active selected minors and full-row-rank terminal factors, the common absorbing row may be rank deficient and has no positive off-exit entries. Neither date \\(4\\) nor time homogeneity is used here.",
    "justification": "The corollary proves exactly what the observable no-date-\\(1\\)-absorption face adds: active masses become positive full masses and at-risk effects become full conditional type effects.",
    "gap": "Existing full-rank reconstruction does not establish this upgrade with a structurally singular common absorbing row and selected \\(J\\)-minors.",
    "consumer": "Full latent-type conditional effects are justified only after the observed panel verifies absence of absorption at the recovery cut.",
